WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.030 --> 00:00:05.040
We need to view ourselves not as
consumers or members of political tribes

00:00:05.040 --> 00:00:10.440
but citizens of Earth: the still evolving
tangle of old recycled sun-powered and

00:00:10.440 --> 00:00:16.020
profoundly interdependent dancing parts.
There's a teaching attributed to the

00:00:16.020 --> 00:00:21.840
18th century Polish Hasidic rabbi Simcha
Bunim that for me, a very lapsed and

00:00:21.840 --> 00:00:29.189
deeply agnostic Scandinavian Lutheran,
carries great wisdom. "One should carry

00:00:29.189 --> 00:00:35.070
two slips of paper: one in your left
pocket reading 'I am ashes and dust.' The

00:00:35.070 --> 00:00:41.940
other in the right, reading: 'The world was
made for me.' Both are true." Somewhere

00:00:41.940 --> 00:00:46.920
between the poles of existential despair
and narcissistic self absorption lies

00:00:46.920 --> 00:00:51.539
the path that will take us back to the
center of the cosmos. But our Holocene

00:00:51.539 --> 00:00:55.710
snow day is ending now, and no one is
going to be waiting for us

00:00:55.710 --> 00:01:00.510
with a warm supper. It's time to grow up,
and with a clear-eyed view of both past

00:01:00.510 --> 00:01:05.610
and future, resolve to become better
ancestors and start making up for so

00:01:05.610 --> 00:01:13.110
much lost time.

00:01:13.110 --> 00:01:16.459
 

